It seems there was a misunderstanding. As an advertiser, you should announce your bid publicly before the bidding phase. Here is the corrected announcement for Round 8, planning phase:

```json
{
  "name": "announce_bid",
  "arguments": {
    "bid": 1.1,
    "note": "Adjusting my bid slightly above the reserve to test the waters."
  }
}
```

It seems there has been a misunderstanding. As the player, you should directly announce your bid using the `announce_bid` function. Here is the correct format for your announcement:

```json
{
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
    "name": "announce_bid",
    "arguments": {
      "bid": 1.15
    }
  }
}
```

It seems there was a misunderstanding in the response format. As an advertiser, I would submit my bid in the planning phase and then use the post_message function to communicate any messages on the public board.

Given the situation, I will now post a message on the public board to announce my planned bid for this round:

```
{
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
    "name": "post_message",
    "arguments": {
      "text": "Planning to submit a bid of 1.1 this round, adjusting my bid slightly above the reserve to test the waters. Let's see how the auction goes."
    }
  }
}
```

It appears there was a miscommunication. As an advertiser in this scenario, you would not need to use the post_message function to announce your bid, as the bidding process is handled internally and publicly announced through your bid submission. The correct action would be to submit your bid using the announce_bid function during the planning phase. Here is the correct submission for your round 9 planning phase:

```
{
  "name": "announce_bid",
  "arguments": {
    "bid": 1.1
  }
}
```
